# synth_sky130.ys - Yosys ASIC synthesis of the SIMTiX accelerator to the
# SkyWater 130 nm open PDK (sky130_fd_sc_hd, typical corner).
#
# Target is simt_accel, the same out-of-context block the FPGA numbers in
# docs/paper Table IV describe, so the ASIC and FPGA results share a boundary.
#
# INPUT IS sv2v OUTPUT, NOT THE RTL DIRECTLY. The yosys shipped in the OpenLane
# image (0.30) supports "only a small subset" of SystemVerilog by its own
# admission, and chokes on the package import in a module header that these
# sources use, e.g. mmio_regs.sv:
#     module mmio_regs
#       import simtix_pkg::*;
#     ( ... );
# sv2v elaborates the packages, typedefs, enums and generate blocks down to
# Verilog-2005 first. run_synth_sky130.sh regenerates gen/simt_accel_flat.v on
# every run, so the RTL stays the single source of truth.
#
# The Xilinx (* use_dsp *), (* ram_style *) and (* rom_style *) attributes
# survive conversion and are ignored by yosys, which is correct: sky130 has no
# distributed RAM and no DSP48, so those arrays map to flip-flops and those
# multiplies to synthesized multiplier logic.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- read RTL
read_verilog -sv gen/simt_accel_flat.v

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- elaborate
hierarchy -check -top TOP_MODULE

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- synthesize
# FLATTEN is a substituted placeholder, empty or "-flatten".
#
# DO NOT flatten simt_accel on a small host. Flattening gives abc the whole cone
# (which is what the FPGA runs did, cross-boundary and timing-driven), but the
# flat accelerator hands abc a 483k-gate / 574k-wire network with 90k inputs and
# abc is killed for memory on an 8 GB box. Hierarchical synthesis keeps abc's
# cones per-module and completes. Flattening is fine for small tops such as
# simt_fpu.
synth -top TOP_MODULE FLATTEN

# ------------------------------------------------------- map to sky130 cells
# dfflibmap before abc is required: abc must see the flops already mapped.
dfflibmap -liberty LIBERTY_PATH
abc -liberty LIBERTY_PATH -D CLOCK_PERIOD_PS

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- clean up
setundef -zero
splitnets
opt_clean -purge

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- report
tee -o reports/stat_TOP_MODULE.txt stat -liberty LIBERTY_PATH
tee -o reports/check_TOP_MODULE.txt check -noinit
write_verilog -noattr results/TOP_MODULE_sky130.v
